n lap 105.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":110,"text":"Three laps later, Hill regained the lead, and the two British World Champions dueled until lap 12, when Hill's BRM appeared alone, and Clark coasted into the pits with a broken piston.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":14},{"lap":110,"text":"He came home twelve seconds ahead for his second win of the year and the completion of a remarkable three-year run at The Glen.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0}]}